    {
      "id": "t2tvdzf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "DEFICITS (MOST IMPORTANT FOR EXAMS)"
    },
    {
      "id": "9jave92",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "REVENUE DEFICIT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Revenue Deficit occurs when:",
      "id": "61ip32n"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "Revenue Expenditure &gt; Revenue Receipts",
      "id": "u0hpxli"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Formula:",
      "id": "wt3rgzj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Revenue Deficit = Revenue Expenditure – Revenue Receipts Meaning:",
      "id": "qy7xp96"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Government is not able to meet its regular expenses.",
      "id": "j39wz1k"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Effect:",
      "id": "ckv6fy6"
    },
    {
      "id": "g5wr4ms",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Bad for economy",
        "Increases debt",
        "Reduces savings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b6f81",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "FISCAL DEFICIT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Fiscal Deficit shows total borrowing requirement of the government. Formula:",
      "id": "wkpxk99"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Fiscal Deficit = Total Expenditure – (Revenue Receipts + Non-debt Capital Receipts)",
      "id": "49urn4v"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Meaning:",
      "id": "y595fzy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It shows how much money government needs to borrow.",
      "id": "0bvgcca"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "High Fiscal Deficit leads to:",
      "id": "gq91fko"
    },
    {
      "id": "ddu45bz",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Inflation",
        "Higher interest rates",
        "More public debt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "idzpsb3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "PRIMARY DEFICIT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Primary Deficit = Fiscal Deficit – Interest Payments",
      "id": "5lrxc4g"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It shows the burden of current year's expenses excluding past loans. If Primary Deficit is zero:",
      "id": "vbemuwx"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "→ Government is managing expenses properly.",
      "id": "0v92vqo"
    },
    {
      "id": "g83zjn6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "DEFICIT FINANCING"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Deficit financing means printing new money or borrowing to meet expenses. Merits:",
      "id": "81ohak0"
    },
    {
      "id": "xfa87eo",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Promotes growth",
        "Helpful in recession"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Deficit Formulas: Revenue Deficit = Revenue Expenditure – Revenue Receipts; Primary Deficit = Fiscal Deficit – Interest Payments.",
        "Fiscal Deficit equals Total Expenditure minus (Revenue Receipts + Non-debt Capital Receipts) and indicates total borrowing requirement.",
        "Article 280 governs the Finance Commission for central-state tax distribution and financial grants.",
        "Distinction between Direct Taxes (Income/Corporate Tax - cannot shift burden) and Indirect Taxes (GST/Customs - can shift burden) is frequently asked."
      ],
      "id": "fw54txq"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Demerits:",
      "id": "qitukyh"
    },
    {
      "id": "q0ez62f",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Causes inflation",
        "Increases debt",
        "Reduces purchasing power"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pkf2jgx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PUBLIC DEBT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Public debt refers to loans taken by the government to meet expenditure. Types:",
